    "narrative": "The LawDog offensive engine for August 31 centers on the trio of **Bryce Harper** (71.42), **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47), and **Dylan Beavers** (66.82). **Bryce Harper** remains our anchor against Brandon Pfaadt, buoyed by a robust .394 xwOBA and a prime #3 slot. **Jonathan Aranda** projects as our most efficient hitter today, as the 4.92 xERA of Stock provides an excellent runway for his dynamic platoon advantage (+12%), while **Dylan Beavers** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+14%) and a high-leverage opportunity to exploit a slow pitcher delivery for stolen base upside. We are also leaning heavily on **Luis Arraez** (66.78) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.05); **Luis Arraez** carries significant BvP equity against Pfaadt, and **Jung Hoo Lee** is uniquely positioned to capitalize on the same stolen base vulnerability against Elder.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card was keeping **JJ Bleday** (48.88) on the bench. Despite a solid projection, he narrowly missed the cut due to a negative platoon split against King, which ultimately pushed him below the threshold required to displace the high-ceiling profiles of **Lawrence Butler** or **Daulton Varsho**. We are keeping a close watch on **Lawrence Butler**, whose score remains suppressed (51.34) by the daunting challenge of facing deGrom; while he carries a strong platoon edge (+13%), the elite arm skill of his opponent makes him a high-variance play today. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Gleyber Torres** (46.98), who is flirting with our \"Marginal\" threshold\u2014his lead-off spot provides utility, but a negative platoon split against Bradley creates a situational risk that limits his overall daily efficiency score.",
